 2. 📚 Most-borrowed books 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: OverDrive/Libby. Chart: Sami Sparber/Axios "The Calamity Club" was last month's most-borrowed e-book on Libby, Axios' Sami Sparber reports. 

 Author Kathryn Stockett's bestseller explores poverty and friendship through the eyes of two outcast women in 1930s Mississippi. 🍿 The big picture: Libby's top 20 features several "BookTok" favorites that have already been adapted for the screen, or are slated to be.

 That includes " Yesteryear " by Caro Claire Burke (a thriller about a tradwife influencer that Anne Hathaway is set to star in and produce) and " The Deal " by Elle Kennedy (the basis for Amazon Prime Video's hit hockey romance series " Off Campus .") Go deeper . 

 
 
